course: dictionary
lesson: 13683
title: Initially and the start of things
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Initially is an adverb. It tells you when something happened: at the beginning, at first, before anything changed. Look for it near the start of a story or a sum. «Initially, the tank held 50 litres of water.» The tank started with 50 litres, and the word tells you that was the starting amount.
explain: Initially can also show that a first plan or idea was changed later. «Initially, Mia wanted pizza, but then she chose soup.» Pizza was her first idea, and soup came later. Ask yourself: is this the first thing, before any change? If yes, initially fits.
explain: Initially is related to the adjective initial, as in «the initial amount». A good check is to swap in «at first» and see if the sentence still makes sense. If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Initially means at the beginning, or at first.
fact: «Initially» can show that a first plan or idea was later changed.
fact: Phrases with the same meaning are «at first», «in the beginning» and «to begin with».
fact: The adjective is initial, so the initial amount is the amount you start with.
fact: In science, the initial state is how things were before an experiment began.
exercise: «Initially, the bucket was empty.» What does initially mean here? | Very quickly | *At the beginning | At the end | Full of water
exercise: «Initially, Sam thought the test was easy, but then it got harder.» What does initially show? | The last thing that happened | *The first idea, which later changed | A loud sound | The answer to the test
exercise: «Initially, there were 12 pencils in the box.» What does initially tell you about the 12? | It was the number of boxes | It was the final number | It was a wrong number | *It was the starting number
test: Which phrase means the same as initially? | Nearly finished | *To begin with | Ending soon | At the back
test: In science, what is the initial state of an experiment? | *How things were before it began | The colour of the results | The name of the lab | How things were after it ended
exam: «Initially the plant was tiny, but after a month it grew tall.» What does initially mean? | Carefully | Very tall | *At the start, before it changed | At the very end
